   "install": {
    "title": "Installation",
    "html": "<h5>Docker</h5>\n<p>The latest image is available on DockerHub at <a href=\"https://hub.docker.com/r/listmonk/listmonk/tags?page=1&amp;ordering=last_updated&amp;name=latest\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><code>listmonk/listmonk:latest</code></a>.\nDownload and use the sample <a href=\"https://github.com/knadh/listmonk/blob/master/docker-compose.yml\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">docker-compose.yml</a>.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-shell\"># Download the compose file to the current directory.\ncurl -LO https://github.com/knadh/listmonk/raw/master/docker-compose.yml\n\n# Run the services in the background.\ndocker compose up -d\n</code></pre>\n<p>Visit <code>http://localhost:9000</code></p>\n<p>See <a href=\"https://listmonk.app/docs/installation\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">installation docs</a></p>\n<hr />\n<h5>Binary</h5>\n<ul>\n<li>Download the <a href=\"https://github.com/knadh/listmonk/releases\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">latest release</a> and extract the listmonk binary.</li>\n<li><code>./listmonk --new-config</code> to generate config.toml. Edit it.</li>\n<li><code>./listmonk --install</code> to setup the Postgres DB (or <code>--upgrade</code> to upgrade an existing DB. Upgrades are idempotent and running them multiple times have no side effects).</li>\n<li>Run <code>./listmonk</code> and visit <code>http://localhost:9000</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>See <a href=\"https://listmonk.app/docs/installation\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">installation docs</a></p>\n<hr />",
